Git-backed incoming evidence application is now exercised end to end through its public step. The new Windows regression task_exchange_windows_incoming_evidence_applies_through_the_public_step_and_replays_offline runs over real confined HTTPS on the dedicated data branch:
- a sender store captures real native evidence under the binding's explicit 95e6 disclosure profile, stages its packs, and commits and pushes;
- a receiver store fetches and retains the commit per operation, then applies through LocalWorkService::task_sync_exchange_step(ApplyEvidence) with explicit opt-in.
It proves:
- original IDs and bytes are retained as imported-only, with no native feed, run or claim credit;
- an exact replay succeeds offline with Git and pack files hidden;
- a changed retry is refused;
- invalid-payload, unenrolled-origin (Dependency) and conflicting-record packs record their original terminal outcomes with no admission, and replay offline.
A small #[cfg(all(test, windows))] storage helper exposes the native sender history and the inertness probes; production visibility is unchanged. Delivered in candidate 48789bd6 (0bd70a30 plus the 98c1 carry plus 95e6, plus 5 test paths). Central GO-CENTRAL-ENGRAM-1DAB-WIN-3 passed (test-c60493bd, 58.5 s) with the candidate's own engram as source owner. Independent evaluation c1cec08ba546479083779d963105f14f passed all 3 criteria. Landing belongs to parent 12325 with the combined freeze.
